      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "The radius of the base of a cylinder is $3\\,\\text{ft}$ and its height is $4\\,\\text{ft}.$ Find the lateral surface area of the cylinder.",
      "worked_solution": "We can calculate the lateral surface area of a cylinder using the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{L}=2\\pi rh,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius and $h$ is the height of the cylinder.\n\nSubstituting $r=3\\,\\text{ft}$ and $h=4\\,\\text{ft}$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{L} & =2\\pi (3)(4)=24\\pi \\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
